`method` on a Go native mark calls the identifier on its first argument.

Without it a native name is emitted as written, with the receiver handed to it
as argument zero: `gfx.Context.Circle(c, 1, 2, 3)`. That is valid Go — a method
expression — but it is not how anyone writes Go, and it is not expressible at
all in a language whose methods are properties of the receiver (see
native_method_js.txtar).

Which shape a host API wants is the API's to say, so it is a flag rather than a
rule: cairo takes its context first and wants the default, a Go method wants
this.

The mark's name keeps its own qualifier, since a Go package's name is not a
function of its import path; the receiver supplies package and type here, so
only the last segment is emitted. `gfx.Reset(c)` in the same output is the
unflagged form, for contrast -- the same declaration shape, called the other
way.

`paint` is called rather than merely declared, because a func nothing calls is
shaken and an archive that shows neither the call nor the declaration asserts
nothing about how either is spelled -- the deny below included.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `Context\.Circle\(` -- the method expression is what the flag replaces
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `func \(m \*main\)` -- the inlined component method is the Model's; `main` is a receiver type this file never declares, and `unverifiable` means no compiler will say so
unverifiable out/go/bubbletea -- imports example.com/gfx, a module written to describe a foreign API and deliberately not published
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import go "sngl:language/go"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

#[go.native("example.com/gfx", "gfx.Context")]
struct Ctx {}

#[go.native("example.com/gfx", "gfx.Context.Circle", method)]
func Ctx.circle(cx float, cy float, r float)

#[go.native("example.com/gfx", "gfx.Reset")]
func reset(c Ctx)

component main() ui.node {
    var n = 0
    var c Ctx

    func paint(c Ctx) {
        c.circle(1.0, 2.0, 3.0)
        reset(c)
    }

    ui.button(text="draw", @click {
        n += 1
        paint(c)
    })
}

ui.window {
    main()
}
-- out/go/bubbletea/model.go --
